  "notes": "Baseline p-chart, the attribute path's stability read (matrix 2.4.3: T-13's continuous orchestrator does not carry proportions; the p-chart branch of T-21 is the baseline route, with T-10's DPMO block as the capability-language half). Selector answered on the record: attribute data, DEFECTIVES -- whole orders pass or fail at the QC desk; the reject log's per-check marks are defects and are charted nowhere here. Subgroups are service days from orders.csv (dataset ref below), n varies 58-90 by day, which is why every point carries its own limits. Frozen from the full 21-day window (>= 20 subgroups, no rule-1/rule-4 signal -- the engine checks both before it will freeze). Center 0.0862 against the customer's half-the-rate ask: stable at a bad level -- nothing special happened on any day; the process is built to reject ~1 order in 12. Armed at freeze: dailies keep landing on this chart until the process itself is changed, and these limits do not move with them.",
